{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1572442522,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MTQ2NzQyMDU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3848","origin":"github"},"title":"download-url -O SUBDIR/ --archive  silently extracts in current (not SUB) dir if SUB not exists","message":"Took me a while to understand what is going on, since some times it was getting extracting under subdir (name was short -- easy to spot a typo), and some times into a current one (name was long, I had a typo in subdir name).\n\n```shell\n$\u003e datalad create -c text2git testds; cd testds;\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/testds \n[INFO   ] Running procedure cfg_text2git                                                                                \n[INFO   ] == Command start (output follows) ===== \n[INFO   ] == Command exit (modification check follows) ===== \ncreate(ok): /tmp/testds (dataset)\n\n$\u003e d=python-novice-inflammation; mkdir -p \"$d\"; datalad download-url -O \"$d\"typo --archive http://swcarpentry.github.io/python-novice-inflammation/data/python-novice-inflammation-data.zip\n[INFO   ] Downloading 'http://swcarpentry.github.io/python-novice-inflammation/data/python-novice-inflammation-data.zip' into 'python-novice-inflammationtypo' \nhttp://swcarpentry.github.io/python-novice-inflammation/data/python-novice-inflammation-data.zip:   0%| | 0.00/22.6k [00                                                                                                                        download_url(ok): python-novice-inflammationtypo (file)\nadd(ok): python-novice-inflammationtypo (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\n[INFO   ] Adding content of the archive python-novice-inflammationtypo into annex \u003cAnnexRepo path=/tmp/testds (\u003cclass 'datalad.support.annexrepo.AnnexRepo'\u003e)\u003e \n[INFO   ] Initiating special remote datalad-archives \n[INFO   ] Finished adding python-novice-inflammationtypo: Files processed: 15, +git: 15 \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  download_url (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n\n$\u003e ls  \ndata/  python-novice-inflammation/\n```\n\nbut it is arguably not a bug per se but side-effect of a feature.  `-O` (as `--help` says) could be used to point to target file name to download to (and that is where the archive gets downloaded to first), and then it gets extracted from current directory:\n\n```shell\n$\u003e git log --stat\ncommit 8a4c958836cc640a7cbff9b4ff2260447cde1776 (HEAD -\u003e master)\nAuthor: Yaroslav Halchenko \u003cdebian@onerussian.com\u003e\nDate:   Wed Oct 30 09:31:29 2019 -0400\n\n    [DATALAD] Added content extracted from archive python-novice-inflammationtypo\n    \n    Files processed: 15\n     +git: 15\n\n data/inflammation-01.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-02.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-03.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-04.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-05.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-06.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-07.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-08.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-09.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-10.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-11.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/inflammation-12.csv       | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n data/small-01.csv              |  2 ++\n data/small-02.csv              |  2 ++\n data/small-03.csv              |  2 ++\n python-novice-inflammationtypo |  1 -\n 16 files changed, 726 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n\ncommit f747339165f8e30b0d22099e1e4552868d3e5b6a\nAuthor: Yaroslav Halchenko \u003cdebian@onerussian.com\u003e\nDate:   Wed Oct 30 09:31:26 2019 -0400\n\n    [DATALAD] Download URLs\n    \n    URLs:\n      http://swcarpentry.github.io/python-novice-inflammation/data/python-novice-inflammation-data.zip\n\n python-novice-inflammationtypo | 1 +\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\n```\n\nso I thought to suggest to throw a warning if `-O` specified together with `--archive` (which would imply extraction), but I feel that could be a reasonable use case as well.\n\nSo not sure if we could/should do anything, or may be someone has an idea?  If not -- we should close this one in a few days. Just wanted to share since was confused for a bit with behavior","files":null}]}